Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||06-02-2000||01:35 AM||||people- i have been set up for a drag race against a 3000GT non turbo. there is a pool of 17 people, most pulling for me- can I win? its a light to light thing, not a full quarter mile. is there anything i can do to milk a few extra ponies from my car? 1987 GT 5spd, K&N, 2.5inch exhaust, high flow cat, flowmaster series40, centerforce dual friction clutch. its a quick car, and i know that a 3kGT is a very heavy car, but thats many years technology difference. honestly, what are my chances, and what can I do? (FYI whether i think i can win or not, i am going to give it my best.)||||reg||1
