Z||000006||CUTTER||06-02-2000||03:47 AM||||if you have AC, unhook it. that will give you a horse or two. What ever you do dont take out the air filter, it takes away alot of acceleration. you can spend $30 and get new accell wires if you dont already have performance wires, if your wires are shady i sugest getting them if you are racing or not. I really hope you take this 3000GT. I raced a early 90 VW GTI 16v 4cyl and lost by a car length later finding out she had NOS.<BR>raced a saturn today and burned him. Never raced a 3000 though, I would love to race one and win. If you want a little better acceleration put the highest octane in with a octane booster, that might give a horse or two. Well I think I rambled enough.<P>Hope this helps, Shane 87GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroSTETZ||06-02-2000||12:32 PM||||anyone ever heard of a ford indigo? believe me or not, i got to ride in one (one of my neighbors works for ford development or something, and i got to attend the unveiling of the concept cars a few years back) i think this car would be rad.. <BR>2300 pounds, 400+hp v12, mid engine, 2 seats. i wonder if that engine would fit in a fiero....<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fikse.com/indy.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fikse.com/indy.html</A> ||||reg||1
